<title>UK: Sun Life says Axa has no plans to buy shares.</title>
<headline>Sun Life says Axa has no plans to buy shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Life &amp; Provincial Holdings Plc said on Wednesday that French insurer Axa SA had confirmed to the company that it had no intention of making an offer for the minority shares in Sun Life.</p>
<p>Axa and fellow French insurer UAP, which owns around 60 percent of Sun Life, announced a merger plan on Tuesday in which Axa is making a share swap offer for UAP.</p>
<p>Sun Life and Provincial Holdings group is made up of life assurance company Sun Life and UAP Provincial.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
